@startuml Topic4_Loop_Control
' ============================================================
' TOPIC 4: Loop Control (keep it safe & bounded)
' EXAM-CRITICAL: turn budget = CODE in orchestration layer,
' NOT a prompt instruction. Never trust the model to self-limit.
' ============================================================
title Topic 4 — Loop Control\n(Bound the loop: termination + turn budget (in CODE) + escalation)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12

start
:Agent loop running (Topic 3);

' ---- The runtime guard wraps every turn ----
partition "ORCHESTRATION / RUNTIME LAYER (real code)" {
  :Increment turn counter;
  if (Turn budget exhausted?\n(e.g. > 10 iterations)) then (YES)
    #Pink:**STOP: budget exhausted**;
    note right
      TURN BUDGET = programmatic guard in CODE.
      * Counts LOOP ITERATIONS (turns), not tokens
      * NOT a polite prompt instruction
      * Never trust the model to limit itself
      * EXAM TRAP: prompt "please stop soon" is WRONG;
        must be enforced in orchestration/runtime code
    end note
    stop
  endif
}

if (External **stop signal** received?) then (YES)
  #Pink:**STOP: stop signal**;
  stop
endif

if (Task complete?\n(termination condition met)) then (YES)
  #LightGreen:**STOP: task complete**;
  stop
endif

if (**Error threshold** crossed?) then (YES)
  #Pink:**STOP: error threshold**;
  stop
endif

' ---- Progress vs spinning detection ----
if (Repeated IDENTICAL tool calls\nAND identical observations?) then (YES = SPINNING)
  #Yellow:Detected: NOT making progress;
  note right
    == PROGRESS vs SPINNING ==
    * Progress = state CHANGES turn to turn
    * Spinning = same call -> same result, repeatedly
    Failure modes that cause infinite loops:
    1. Missing stop condition
    2. Always-failing tool (retries forever)
    3. Circular reasoning
  end note
  if (Authorization boundary /\nMissing info /\nHuman judgment needed?) then (YES)
    #LightBlue:**ESCALATE** to human / higher authority;
    note left
      Escalation = DESIGNED SAFETY VALVE, not a failure.
      Escalate at: authorization boundary,
      missing information it can't get,
      or need for human judgment.
    end note
    stop
  else (NO — recoverable)
    :Adjust approach and continue;
  endif
else (NO — real progress)
  :Continue to next turn (loop back to Topic 3);
endif

stop

floating note left
  == FOUR CLEAN STOP REASONS ==
  1. Task complete
  2. Error threshold crossed
  3. Budget exhausted
  4. External stop signal
  ----
  == ITERATE vs ESCALATE ==
  Iterate (try again yourself) by default.
  Escalate only at: authorization boundary /
  missing info / human judgment required.
end note

@enduml
